      3 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لادّهُ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لِدَادٌ</span> (A, Msb) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُلَادَّةٌ</span>, (A,)
<i>He contended with him violently,</i> or <i>vehemently,
in an altercation; in a dispute; in a litigation.</i>
(A, Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا زِلْتُ أُلَادُّ عَنْكَ</span> <i>I ceased not to
repel from thee;</i> or, <i>to defend thee.</i> (S.)

